ul.li:
Code Readability


Descriptive variables. For example: instead of using Vector3 a = new Vector3(b.x,0,b.z); you can use Vector3 flattenedPos = new Vector3(pos.x, 0, pos.y); This will help everyone around you understand what the variable is.

Commenting. When commenting try to comment why the code exists and not what it does. The code should explain what it does. Why does it exist and what is its purpose?

Summaries. Similar to comments these are to explain your variables and methods. instead of // use /// right before the method or variable to start a summary. This is what creates the description of what it does once you hover over the method name.




